Here is a structured overview and design specification for the **Project Design Phase** of the [LegalEase-AI-Powered-Legal-Document-Generator](https://github.com/divyasrins2007-ux/LegalEase-AI-Powered-Legal-Document-Generator?utm_source=gemini):

---

## 1. System Architecture & High-Level Design

### Core Components

* **Frontend UI Client:** Next.js / React single-page application handling dynamic form rendering, live document previews, and real-time chat interactions with AI.
* **Backend API Layer:** FastAPI / Node.js service managing authentication, workflow orchestration, database queries, and document processing jobs.
* **AI Orchestration Engine:** Integrates with LLM APIs (OpenAI / Anthropic) for prompt handling, structured variable extraction, risk analysis, and dynamic document modifications.
* **Document Rendering Engine:** Engine converting dynamic JSON structures or Markdown templates into populated `.docx` and `.pdf` files.
* **Database & Storage:** PostgreSQL / Supabase for user state, session persistence, template storage, and document metadata; S3-compatible storage for generated document files.

---

## 2. User Interface (UI) & User Experience (UX) Design

### Wireframe Layout & Workflows

* **Dashboard:** Shows document history, saved drafts, template library, and quick-start actions.
* **Dynamic Questionnaire Interface:** Step-by-step form wizard featuring real-time input validation, contextual help tooltips, and dynamic logic branching (showing conditional inputs based on previous selections).
* **Split-View Document Editor:**
* *Left Panel:* Conversational AI prompt interface & structured form controls for dynamic edits.
* *Right Panel:* Live visual document preview with highlighted changes and plain-English risk flag annotations.


* **Export & Share Modal:** Download choices (`.docx`, `.pdf`) alongside permission/sharing settings.

---

## 3. Database Schema & Data Modeling

### Core Entities

* **Users:** `id`, `email`, `name`, `role`, `created_at`
* **Templates:** `id`, `title`, `category`, `base_content`, `variable_schema` (JSON definition of inputs required)
* **Documents:** `id`, `user_id`, `template_id`, `form_data` (JSON), `generated_content`, `status`, `created_at`
* **Audit Trail / Revision History:** `id`, `document_id`, `prompt_history`, `version_number`, `created_at`

---

## 4. API & Data Flow Design

```
[ User Input / Prompt ] ---> [ Next.js Frontend ] 
                                  |
                                  v
                         [ FastAPI Backend ]
                           /            \
                          v              v
            [ Database / Storage ]   [ LLM Engine / Prompt Pipeline ]
                          \              /
                           v            v
                    [ Generated Document Draft ]
                                  |
                                  v
                   [ Render Engine (.docx / .pdf) ]

```

### Key API Endpoints

* `POST /api/templates`: Fetch templates and variable schema for a given legal document type.
* `POST /api/documents/generate`: Accept user responses, process via LLM template engine, and return generated draft.
* `POST /api/documents/edit-clause`: Process natural language revision prompts to adjust specific clauses in the draft.
* `GET /api/documents/{id}/export?format=pdf|docx`: Generate downloadable file payload.
